  "form": "Problem note",
  "pages": 17,
  "question": "Which Mersenne-support subseries are settled, what finite-period and achievement-set structure is proved, and what still blocks Erdős #257?",
  "precis": "Fix a finite nonempty prime set P and put h(a)=∏_{p∈P}p^{v_p(a)}. If an infinite support A has ∑_{a∈A}h(a)/(a(2^{h(a)}−1)) finite, its reciprocal Mersenne subseries is irrational at every integer base b≥2, as is the subseries on every infinite subset of A. The paper prints a complete ordinary proof and a host with divergent reciprocal sum, so the criterion is strictly weaker than reciprocal summability. A common observation window also proves hereditary irrationality for unions of weighted supports and strengthened positive-cover supports. These are ordinary results, not Lean theorems, and no priority claim is made. Universal Erdős #257 remains open.",
  "owns": "problem-specific mathematical exposition for Erdős #257: exact finite-prime weighted support criterion, mixed weighted-and-cover support theorem and their ordinary proofs, exact finite periods, settled support families, method limits, and the open half-value edge",
